WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.709 --> 00:00:15.729
hurried down the street.

2
00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.431
"Come on, Kaleem!

3
00:00:18.671 --> 00:00:19.991
We need to find the monster."

4
00:00:20.011 --> 00:00:23.133
"Wait," Kaleem said.

5
00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.494
"Didn't we promise to walk Finn today?"

6
00:00:26.774 --> 00:00:29.515
Daisy stopped, glad he had remembered that.

7
00:00:29.535 --> 00:00:31.056
"Let's go get Finn.

8
00:00:32.212 --> 00:00:34.533
Maybe he can help us with this investigation."

9
00:00:38.755 --> 00:00:40.276
They hurried toward Finn's house.

10
00:00:40.296 --> 00:00:44.137
"Are you sure you understood what the animals said, Daisy?"

11
00:00:44.537 --> 00:00:45.358
Kaleem asked.

12
00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.959
"It sounds like they were describing totally different monsters."

13
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.840
"That's true."

14
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.621
Daisy thought for a second.

15
00:00:52.641 --> 00:00:55.982
"One said the monster was shaggy like a bear.

16
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:59.304
Another said it had a long neck like a snake."

17
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:01.993
Kaleem nodded.

18
00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:06.597
"And it roars and shoots poison from its mouth, and it's as big as a house.

19
00:01:07.518 --> 00:01:11.281
Either the animals saw different things, or it's definitely a monster."

20
00:01:11.301 --> 00:01:16.686
"It's not a monster," Daisy said for what felt like the millionth time.

21
00:01:16.706 --> 00:01:19.508
"But I suppose they could have seen different things."

22
00:01:19.528 --> 00:01:24.552
"The shaggy creature could be a large dog," Kaleem said.

23
00:01:24.572 --> 00:01:28.456
"And the spitting creature could be a kid with a water blaster."

24
00:01:29.584 --> 00:01:31.065
"No," Daisy said.

25
00:01:31.085 --> 00:01:33.566
"These animals know what a dog is.

26
00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.008
They wouldn't mix up a dog and a monster.

27
00:01:37.088 --> 00:01:39.029
Not even a big, shaggy one."

28
00:01:47.414 --> 00:01:50.435
Soon they were walking down the sidewalk with lively Finn.

29
00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:52.477
"Woof! Woof!"

30
00:01:54.257 --> 00:01:56.419
Finn jumped around like he always did.

31
00:01:56.439 --> 00:01:58.520
"There's a monster?

32
00:01:59.024 --> 00:02:00.525
Really? That's so cool!

33
00:02:01.265 --> 00:02:02.326
Or maybe it's scary.

34
00:02:02.906 --> 00:02:05.367
Or maybe it's cool and scary!"

35
00:02:05.387 --> 00:02:07.928
"Can you help us track it, Finn?"

36
00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:08.949
Daisy said.

37
00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:11.410
"You like smelling things, right?"

38
00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.411
"Yes! I have the best nose around!"

39
00:02:14.911 --> 00:02:16.012
Finn said proudly.

40
00:02:22.034 --> 00:02:25.036
They went back to the spot where the beagle had seen the monster.

41
00:02:30.188 --> 00:02:30.969
"Hey, how's it going?"

42
00:02:31.329 --> 00:02:32.750
Finn barked excitedly.

43
00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.511
"Want to play with me?"

44
00:02:35.351 --> 00:02:37.333
The beagle was lying under a table.

45
00:02:37.913 --> 00:02:39.835
His voice shook nervously.

46
00:02:39.855 --> 00:02:42.116
"No, I'm too scared to play.

47
00:02:42.136 --> 00:02:44.257
There's a monster around here!"

48
00:02:44.278 --> 00:02:47.039
"Come on, Finn," Daisy said.

49
00:02:47.059 --> 00:02:49.201
"Let's explore this neighborhood.

50
00:02:50.181 --> 00:02:52.643
We need to find out what's scaring all the animals."

51
00:02:53.564 --> 00:02:54.965
"Oh, right," Finn said.

52
00:02:54.985 --> 00:02:57.727
"Don't worry, buddy," he said to the beagle.

53
00:02:57.747 --> 00:02:59.548
"We'll figure out this mystery."

54
00:03:01.344 --> 00:03:03.786
Finn stuck his nose on the ground and sniffed.

55
00:03:04.566 --> 00:03:07.188
His tail stiffened, and his eyes widened.

56
00:03:07.208 --> 00:03:09.850
"Whoa!" he cried.

57
00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.572
"I've never smelled anything like this!"

58
00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:17.915
"That's because we've never had a monster around here," the beagle said.

59
00:03:17.935 --> 00:03:20.036
"I smelled it too.

60
00:03:21.197 --> 00:03:23.299
It was like nothing I'd ever smelled either.

61
00:03:24.039 --> 00:03:26.241
And I've smelled a lot of things!"

62
00:03:28.842 --> 00:03:31.104
Daisy told Kaleem what the dogs were saying.

63
00:03:32.972 --> 00:03:34.373
"Can Finn follow the trail?"

64
00:03:34.793 --> 00:03:35.653
Kaleem asked.

65
00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:38.214
"Sure I can!"

66
00:03:40.195 --> 00:03:42.636
Finn rushed forward with his nose to the ground.

67
00:03:43.057 --> 00:03:44.977
Daisy was pulled along by the leash.

68
00:03:49.059 --> 00:03:49.920
down, Finn!"

69
00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.580
she called with a laugh.

70
00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.342
"I can't run as fast as you can!"

71
00:03:54.362 --> 00:03:59.624
"Sorry." Finn sniffed.

72
00:04:02.556 --> 00:04:03.556
"It went this way!"

73
00:04:08.258 --> 00:04:11.299
They followed Finn's nose down the block and around the corner.

74
00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:20.942
The trail kept going.

75
00:04:26.263 --> 00:04:28.164
The houses got farther apart.

76
00:04:30.432 --> 00:04:33.213
Finally Finn's nose led them to a gate.

77
00:04:34.994 --> 00:04:37.576
A sign read Our Little Farm.

78
00:04:37.596 --> 00:04:40.337
"The smell goes right through the gate."

79
00:04:40.837 --> 00:04:42.058
Finn wagged his tail.

80
00:04:42.078 --> 00:04:45.860
"The monster is at this farm!"
